# Target C: close the eight-no-root k=4, D=-2, d_root=0, p=2 branch

Date: 2026-09-26

Status: exact support-level closure of the remaining eight-no-root k=4,D=-2 arithmetic branch. This is a finite support-seven/global-segment result. It does not close the two D=-1,k=4 branches, Target C-II, or Erdos Problem #99.

Companion verifier:

research/verify_target_c_support7_global_segment_relative_eight_noroot_k4_dminus2_d0p2_support_closure_2026_09_26.py

## Inputs

The preceding k=4 reduction and weight sharpening give rank(P)=4 and generalized weights

(d1,d2,d3,d4)(P) >= (4,5,6,7)

for this D=-2,d_root=0,p=2 branch.

The selected incomplete-root cost p=2 has exactly two profiles, apart from any actual-empty blocks: one selected pair block, or two selected singleton blocks.

For an actual-empty touched triangle block b, the committed local-block rule gives dim(E_b)=2 iff some containing tetrahedral four-support occurs at least twice among the eight no-root cycles; otherwise dim(E_b)=1.

The committed face-local four-cycle identity, together with the singleton/pair local-kernel facts and E_b <= P for actual-empty blocks, puts every external relation lift in H(T), the span of the touched triangle rows. This is the same containment used in research/target_c_support7_global_segment_relative_eight_noroot_k5_dminus1_d0p6_two_singleton_split_2026-09-25.md.

Because d_root=0, all complete-root triangle rows are independent.

## A universal touched-block bound

Let h be the number of touched triangle blocks, e the number of touched actual-empty blocks, and t the number of touched selected singleton/pair blocks. Here t<=2.

The touched complete blocks are an independent subset of the 15-dimensional ground-root space, so there are at most 15 of them. Hence

e >= h-15-t >= h-17.

Every actual-empty block has at least four incident external coordinates: a rank-one empty constraint uses d1>=4, while a rank-two empty constraint uses d2>=5. Every other touched block has at least one incidence. The eight no-root cycles contribute exactly 32 cycle-block incidences. Therefore

32 >= 4e+(h-e)=h+3e >= 4h-51,

so h<=20.

Thus every support multiset touching at least 21 triangle blocks is impossible before phase or relation-rank work.

## Generalized-weight support filters

For a touched block b, let I_b be the set of external-cycle occurrences touching it. The actual coordinate support of its local coefficient space is contained in I_b. Using I_b therefore weakens the following tests and makes them necessary conditions.

An actual-empty block is individually possible only when

- dim(E_b)=1 and |I_b|>=4, or
- dim(E_b)=2 and |I_b|>=5.

For two nonzero local spaces supported inside occurrence sets I,J, the generalized weights imply:

- line-line: |I intersect J|>=4 or |I union J|>=5;
- plane-line: |I intersect J|>=4 or |I union J|>=6;
- plane-plane: |I intersect J|>=5, or both |I intersect J|>=4 and |I union J|>=6, or |I union J|>=7.

These are obtained by splitting according to intersection dimension and applying d1,d2,d3,d4 to the intersection or sum.

P is generated by the actual-empty spaces and the nonzero singleton lines; a selected pair contributes no coefficient constraint. Since d4(P)>=7, the union of the coordinate supports of these generators must contain at least seven of the eight external coordinates. The verifier again checks only the larger incidence sets I_b.

For touched singleton blocks the verifier deliberately permits the local singleton constraint to be zero. If declared nonzero, it is only treated as a line supported in I_b and must have |I_b|>=4. This enlarges the search beyond actual realizations.

## Complete-root independence and face-local capacity

For a candidate touched incomplete set I inside T, let C=T minus I. The triangle rows in C must be independent because d_root=0.

Write

nu(T)=|T|-rank H(T).

The defect identity is

D = 8+p+3d_root-3k = 8+2-12 = -2.

If c is the number of actual complete-root blocks, the full relation rank is c+4. The complete-root rows already have rank c, so all four external nullspace directions must survive independently modulo the complete-root span.

Every external lift lies in H(T). Passing from the full complete-root span to the smaller touched-complete span can only increase quotient rank. Therefore a necessary condition is

4 <= rank H(T)-rank H(C).

Because C is independent, this becomes

|I|-nu(T) >= 4.

The verifier computes these triangle-row ranks exactly. It also performs a redundant tetrahedron-boundary injectivity check: restriction of the span of the distinct tetrahedron-boundary dependencies to I must be injective, since a nonzero dependency supported entirely on C would contradict complete-row independence.

## Exact support census

Ignore cycle orientations and keep only the multiset of the eight underlying tetrahedral four-supports on seven vertices. There are 35 possible supports, and support multiplicity is at most three because each support has only three distinct no-root four-cycles.

The committed p=6,e=8 support verifier independently certified, by Burnside counting and canonical augmentation, the S7 orbit counts for support-multiset sizes zero through eight:

1,1,4,14,61,268,1283,6032,27763.

The new verifier runs the same canonical augmentation and asserts this count sequence. Among the 27,763 size-eight orbits, 13,574 touch at most 20 triangle blocks and survive the incidence bound.

For each of those 13,574 orbits, the verifier exhaustively enumerates every pairwise-compatible set of individually eligible actual-empty blocks, then tests both p=2 profiles:

- one selected pair, allowing the pair to be touched or untouched;
- two selected singletons, allowing zero, one, or both to be touched and allowing a touched singleton local constraint to vanish whenever helpful.

It imposes only the necessary conditions above. It does not enumerate phases and does not require the nominal local spaces to glue to an actual rank-four P. Hence it scans a strict superset of actual states.

The executed certificate gives

support_multiset_orbits_size_8 = 27763
touch_at_most_20 = 13574
pair_profile_survivors = 0
two_singleton_profile_survivors = 0

Therefore no support multiset can realize this branch.

## Exactness of rank decisions

Support canonicalization and incidence tests use exact integer/set arithmetic.

Triangle and tetrahedron-boundary ranks are computed modulo 2^31-1. The verifier runs the Lucas-Lehmer test for this prime. Triangle rows have squared norm 3; tetrahedron-boundary rows have squared norm 4. Triangle-row rank is at most 15, and at most eight tetrahedron-boundary rows occur here. The verifier checks

(2^31-1)^2 > 4^15.

Hadamard's inequality therefore bounds every relevant nonzero integer minor strictly below the prime in absolute value. Reduction modulo the prime cannot destroy a nonzero rational minor, so all modular ranks used by the certificate equal their rational ranks.

## Conclusion

There is no eight-no-root state with

k=4, D=-2, d_root=0, p=2.

The eight-no-root k=4 frontier is now reduced to the two D=-1 branches

(d_root,p)=(0,3) and (1,0).

This result does not claim closure of either D=-1 branch, Target C-II, or Erdos Problem #99.
